course: dictionary
lesson: 6926
title: A promise you can count on
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pact is a serious promise or agreement that people make together. It can be between friends, between groups, or even between countries. When you read pact, look for the clue: someone has agreed to do something, and both sides are meant to keep their word.
explain: «Ben and his big brother had blamed each other for years; one day they made a pact: "No more blaming."» Pact must mean a promise, because they agreed to stop blaming each other. Check it: put promise in the place of pact, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look at what happens after the word. «Ollie and Jayden made a pact — no loot boxes this term — and saved enough to buy a whole new game together.» The pact was a promise they kept, and keeping it helped them reach a goal.
explain: Countries can make pacts too. NATO countries promise to defend each other, so their pact is an agreement that changes how they act. When you meet pact, ask yourself: who is promising, and what are they promising?
fact: A pact is a serious agreement or promise.
fact: A pact can be made by people, groups or countries.
fact: A pact can also be a secret promise between friends, such as «We made a pact to never tell».
fact: In old tales, a «pact with the devil» is a dangerous bargain.
exercise: «Ben and his big brother made a pact: "No more blaming."» What is a pact here? | A game they play after school | A fight that ends in tears | *A promise they both agree to keep | A large family dinner
exercise: NATO countries promise to defend each other. What kind of agreement is this? | *A pact | A diary | A puzzle | A lullaby
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «Ollie and Jayden made a pact — no loot boxes this term» that means a serious promise. | Jayden | *pact | term | loot
test: «Ollie and Jayden made a pact — no loot boxes this term.» What does pact mean here? | *A serious promise they both agree to keep | A rule for games | A snack break | A map of the town
test: Mia says, «We made a pact to never tell.» What does pact suggest? | A holiday trip | *A secret promise between friends | A new bike | A loud argument
exam: Which of these describes a pact? | A quick sneeze | A single loud noise | A small pile of leaves | *A serious promise or agreement between people, groups or countries
